# What a container build (Dockerfile, ADR-0009) may read. A build on a developer's machine would send this
# directory to Docker, so everything local-only stays out: env files with real secrets above all (SECURITY T41).

# env files, including the untracked root .env of the legacy app; the image needs none of them
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# version control, editor and assistant settings
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.pem

# dependencies and build output: the image installs and builds its own
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo
packages/db/src/generated
**/next-env.d.ts

# caches, reports and local data
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/coverage-integration
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.drift
packages/bench/fixtures/.cache
packages/bench/results
